### MEDUSA submission rate limiting
# Use REST Client with a valid participant token and a challenge/team from the submissions walkthrough.
# Run requests repeatedly. A successful response consumes the general per-user request budget.
# Incorrect flags also consume the shared team+challenge incorrect-attempt budget.
# After the configured limit, expect HTTP 429 and a Retry-After header.
# If Redis is unavailable, submission requests fail closed with HTTP 503.
# The defaults are 60 submission requests per user per 60 seconds and 10 incorrect
# attempts per team/challenge per 60 seconds. Both are configurable via environment.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000/api/v1
@token = replace-with-participant-access-token
@challengeId = 1
@teamId = 1

### Submit an incorrect flag repeatedly to test the incorrect-attempt limit
POST {{baseUrl}}/challenges/{{challengeId}}/submissions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "team_id": {{teamId}},
  "flag": "MEDUSA{intentionally_wrong_flag}"
}

### General request limit: repeat the request above more than the configured
# SUBMISSION_REQUEST_LIMIT within SUBMISSION_RATE_WINDOW_SECONDS.
